](http://om.rs/o3ui))\\n- [x] My work includes tests or is validated by existing tests.\\n- [x] I have updated the esm-framework and storybook mocks ([mock.tsx](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/mock.tsx), [mock-jest.tsx](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/mock-jest.tsx), and [storybook mocks](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/tooling/storybook/mocks/)) to reflect any API changes.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThe login app declares `chooseLocation.locationsPerRequest` and `chooseLocation.numberToShow` in its config schema, but neither value was read anywhere. The shared `LocationPicker` from the styleguide always used its default page size of 50, so setting `locationsPerRequest` in a distro config had no effect.\\n\\nThis PR:\\n\\n* Passes `chooseLocation.locationsPerRequest` to `LocationPicker`, so the configured page size is used for the FHIR `Location` requests and for the infinite scroll trigger.\\n* Removes `chooseLocation.numberToShow`. It comes from the fixed-length location list that predates infinite scroll and has no equivalent in the current picker. Implementations that still set it will see a single `Unknown config key` console error until they remove it; nothing else changes, since the option was already ignored.\\n* Deletes the unused `useLoginLocations` hook from `login.resource.ts`. It was a stale copy of the styleguide hook and was not imported by anything in this repo. The login app is not consumable as a library, and a GitHub code search finds no external imports of it.\\n\\nA test covers the new behaviour: with `locationsPerRequest: 5` in config, `LocationPicker` receives `locationsPerRequest: 5`.\\n\\nOnly the login app's own `__mocks__/config.mock.ts` needed updating. The framework and storybook mocks do not reference these keys.\\n\\n## Screenshots\\n\\nNo UI changes.\\n\\n## Related Issue\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Other\\n\\n